#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.48 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:10
msgid ""
"A new configuration variable remote.<name>.serverOption makes the transport "
"layer act as if the --serverOption=<value> option is given from the command "
"line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:13
msgid ""
"\"git rebase --rebase-merges\" now uses branch names as labels when able."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:15
msgid "Describe the policy to introduce breaking changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:18
msgid ""
"Teach 'git notes add' and 'git notes append' a new '-e' flag, instructing "
"them to open the note in $GIT_EDITOR before saving."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:21
msgid ""
"Documentation for \"git bundle\" saw improvements to more prominently call "
"out the use of '--all' when creating bundles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:23
msgid "Drop support for older libcURL and Perl."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:26
msgid ""
"End-user experience of \"git mergetool\" when the command errors out has "
"been improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:30
msgid ""
"\"git bundle --unbundle\" and \"git clone\" running on a bundle file both "
"learned to trigger fsck over the new objects with configurable fck check "
"levels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:34
msgid ""
"When \"git fetch $remote\" notices that refs/remotes/$remote/HEAD is missing "
"and discovers what branch the other side points with its HEAD, refs/remotes/"
"$remote/HEAD is updated to point to it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:37
msgid ""
"\"git fetch\" honors \"remote.<remote>.followRemoteHEAD\" settings to tweak "
"the remote-tracking HEAD in \"refs/remotes/<remote>/HEAD\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:41
msgid ""
"\"git range-diff\" learned to optionally show and compare merge commits in "
"the ranges being compared, with the --diff-merges option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:47
msgid "Document \"amlog\" notes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:51
msgid ""
"The way AsciiDoc is used for SYNOPSIS part of the manual pages has been "
"revamped.  The sources, at least for the simple cases, got vastly more "
"pleasant to work with."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:55
msgid ""
"The reftable library is now prepared to expect that the memory allocation "
"function given to it may fail to allocate and to deal with such an error."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:59
msgid ""
"An extra worktree attached to a repository points at each other to allow "
"finding the repository from the worktree (and vice versa)  possible.  Use "
"relative paths for this linkage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:61
msgid "Enable Windows-based CI in GitLab."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Commands that can also work outside Git have learned to take the repository "
"instance \"repo\" when we know we are in a repository, and NULL when we are "
"not, in a parameter.  The uses of the_repository variable in a few of them "
"have been removed using the new calling convention."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:71
msgid ""
"The reftable sub-system grew a new reftable-specific strbuf replacement to "
"reduce its dependency on Git-specific data structures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:74
msgid ""
"The ref-filter machinery learns to recognize and avoid cases where sorting "
"would be redundant."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:77
msgid ""
"Various platform compatibility fixes split out of the larger effort to use "
"Meson as the primary build tool."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Treat ECONNABORTED the same as ECONNRESET in 'git credential-cache' to work "
"around a possible Cygwin regression. This resolves a race condition caused "
"by changes in Cygwin's handling of socket closures, allowing the client to "
"exit cleanly when encountering ECONNABORTED."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:85
msgid "Demonstrate an assertion failure in 'git mv'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:88
msgid ""
"Documentation update to clarify that 'uploadpack.allowAnySHA1InWant' implies "
"both 'allowTipSHA1InWant' and 'allowReachableSHA1InWant'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:91
msgid ""
"Replace various calls to atoi() with strtol_i() and strtoul_ui(), and add "
"improved error handling."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:93
msgid "Documentation updates to 'git-update-ref(1)'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:96
msgid ""
"Update the project's CodingGuidelines to discourage naming functions with a "
"\"_1()\" suffix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:98
msgid "Update '.clang-format' to match project conventions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:100
msgid "Centralize documentation for repository extensions into a single place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:102
msgid "Buildfix and upgrade of Clar to a newer version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:104
msgid "Documentation mark-up updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:106
msgid "Renaming a handful of variables and structure fields."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:108
msgid "Fix for clar unit tests to support CMake build."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:110
msgid "C23 compatibility updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:112
msgid "GCC 15 compatibility updates."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:115
msgid ""
"We now ensure \"index-pack\" is used with the \"--promisor\" option only "
"during a \"git fetch\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:117
msgid "The migration procedure between two ref backends has been optimized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:122
msgid ""
"\"git fsck\" learned to issue warnings on \"curiously formatted\" ref "
"contents that have always been treated as valid but that Git wouldn't have "
"written itself (e.g., missing terminating end-of-line after the full object "
"name)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:124
msgid "Work around Coverity warning that would not trigger in practice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:127
msgid ""
"Built-in Git subcommands are supplied the repository object to work with; "
"they learned to do the same when they invoke sub-subcommands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:129
msgid "Drop support for ancient environments in various CI jobs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:132
msgid ""
"Isolate the reftable subsystem from the rest of Git's codebase by using "
"fewer pieces of Git's infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:135
msgid ""
"Optimize reading random references out of the reftable backend by allowing "
"reuse of iterator objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:137
msgid "Backport oss-fuzz tests to our codebase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:140
msgid ""
"Introduce a new repository extension to prevent older Git versions from mis-"
"interpreting worktrees created with relative paths."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:142
msgid "Yet another \"pass the repository through the callchain\" topic."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:145
msgid "\"git describe\" learned to stop digging the history needlessly deeper."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:147
msgid "Build procedure update plus introduction of Meson based builds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:151
msgid ""
"Recent reftable updates mistook a NULL return from a request for 0-byte "
"allocation as OOM and died unnecessarily, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:153
msgid "Reftable backend adds check for upper limit of log's update_index."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:155
msgid "Start working to make the codebase buildable with -Wsign-compare."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:157
msgid "Regression fix for 'show-index' when run outside of a repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:160
msgid ""
"The meson-build procedure is integrated into CI to catch and prevent "
"bitrotting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:163
msgid ""
"\"git refs migrate\" learned to also migrate the reflog data across backends."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:166
msgid ""
"The developer documentation has been updated to give the latest info on gitk "
"and git-gui maintainer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:170
msgid ""
"CI jobs that run threaded programs under LSan has been giving false "
"positives from time to time, which has been worked around."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:173
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.47"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:177
msgid ""
"Doc update to clarify how periodical maintenance are scheduled, spread "
"across time to avoid thundering herds."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:180
msgid ""
"Use after free and double freeing at the end in \"git log -L... -p\" had "
"been identified and fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:184
msgid ""
"On macOS, fsmonitor can fall into a race condition that results in a client "
"waiting forever to be notified about an event that has already happened.  "
"This problem has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:187
msgid ""
"\"git maintenance start\" crashed due to an uninitialized variable "
"reference, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:190
msgid ""
"Fail gracefully instead of crashing when attempting to write the contents of "
"a corrupt in-core index as a tree object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:194
msgid ""
"A \"git fetch\" from the superproject going down to a submodule used a wrong "
"remote when the default remote names are set differently between them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:196
msgid "Fixes compile time warnings with 64-bit MSVC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:199
msgid ""
"Teaches 'shortlog' to explicitly use SHA-1 when operating outside of a "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:202
msgid ""
"Fix 'git grep' regression on macOS by disabling lookahead when encountering "
"invalid UTF-8 byte sequences."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:207
msgid ""
"The dumb-http code regressed when the result of re-indexing a pack yielded "
"an *.idx file that differs in content from the *.idx file it downloaded from "
"the remote. This has been corrected by no longer relying on the *.idx file "
"we got from the remote."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:211
msgid ""
"When called with '--left-right' and '--use-bitmap-index', 'rev-list' will "
"produce output without any left/right markers, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:213
msgid "More leakfixes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:215
msgid "Test modernization."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:218
msgid ""
"The \"--shallow-exclude=<ref>\" option to various history transfer commands "
"takes a ref, not an arbitrary revision."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:222
msgid ""
"A regression where commit objects missing from a commit-graph can cause an "
"infinite loop when doing a fetch in a partial clone has been fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:226
msgid ""
"The MinGW compatibility layer has been taught to support POSIX semantics for "
"atomic renames when other process(es) have a file opened at the destination "
"path."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:232
msgid ""
"\"git gc\" discards any objects that are outside promisor packs that are "
"referred to by an object in a promisor pack, and we do not refetch them from "
"the promisor at runtime, resulting an unusable repository.  Work around it "
"by including these objects in the referring promisor pack at the receiving "
"end of the fetch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:236
msgid ""
"Avoid build/test breakage on a system without working malloc debug support "
"dynamic library.  (merge 72ad6dc368 jk/test-malloc-debug-check later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:239
msgid ""
"Double-free fix.  (merge fe17a25905 jk/fetch-prefetch-double-free-fix later "
"to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:242
msgid ""
"Use of some uninitialized variables in \"git difftool\" has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:246
msgid ""
"Object reuse code based on multi-pack-index sent an unwanted copy of "
"object.  (merge e199290592 tb/multi-pack-reuse-dupfix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:250
msgid ""
"\"git fast-import\" can be tricked into a replace ref that maps an object to "
"itself, which is a useless thing to do.  (merge 5e904f1a4a en/fast-import-"
"avoid-self-replace later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:254
msgid ""
"The ref-transaction hook triggered for reflog updates, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge b886db48c6 kn/ref-transaction-hook-with-reflog later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:258
msgid ""
"Give a bit of advice/hint message when \"git maintenance\" stops finding a "
"lock file left by another instance that still is potentially running.  "
"(merge ba874d1dac ps/gc-stale-lock-warning later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:261
msgid ""
"Use the right helper program to measure file size in performance tests.  "
"(merge 3f97f1bce6 tb/use-test-file-size-more later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:265
msgid ""
"A double-free that may not trigger in practice by luck has been corrected in "
"the reference resolution code.  (merge b6318cf23a sj/refs-symref-referent-"
"fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:267
msgid "The sequencer failed to honor core.commentString in some places."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:271
msgid ""
"Describe a case where an option value needs to be spelled as a separate "
"argument, i.e. \"--opt val\", not \"--opt=val\".  (merge 1bc1e94091 jc/doc-"
"opt-tilde-expand later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:276
msgid ""
"Loosen overly strict ownership check introduced in the recent past, to keep "
"the promise \"cloning a suspicious repository is a safe first step to "
"inspect it\".  (merge 0ffb5a6bf1 bc/allow-upload-pack-from-other-people "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:280
msgid ""
"\"git fast-import\" learned to reject paths with \"..\" and \".\" as their "
"components to avoid creating invalid tree objects.  (merge 8cb4c6e62f en/"
"fast-import-verify-path later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:284
msgid ""
"The --ancestry-path option is designed to be given a commit that is on the "
"path, which was not documented, which has been corrected.  (merge bc1a980759 "
"kk/doc-ancestry-path later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:289
msgid ""
"\"git tag\" has been taught to refuse to create refs/tags/HEAD since such a "
"tag will be confusing in the context of the UI provided by the Git Porcelain "
"commands.  (merge bbd445d5ef jc/forbid-head-as-tagname later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:293
msgid ""
"The advice messages now tell the newer 'git config set' command to set the "
"advice.token configuration variable to squelch a message.  (merge 6c397d0104 "
"bf/explicit-config-set-in-advice-messages later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:297
msgid ""
"The syntax \":/<text>\" to name the latest commit with the matching text was "
"broken with a recent change, which has been corrected.  (merge 0ff919e87a ps/"
"commit-with-message-syntax-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:300
msgid ""
"Fix performance regression of a recent \"fatten promisor pack with local "
"objects\" protection against an unwanted gc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:303
msgid ""
"\"git log -p --remerge-diff --reverse\" was completely broken.  (merge "
"f94bfa1516 js/log-remerge-keep-ancestry later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:308
msgid ""
"\"git bundle create\" with an annotated tag on the positive end of the "
"revision range had a workaround code for older limitation in the revision "
"walker, which has become unnecessary.  (merge dd1072dfa8 tc/bundle-with-tag-"
"remove-workaround later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:311
msgid ""
"GitLab CI updates.  (merge c6b43f663e ps/ci-gitlab-update later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:315
msgid ""
"Code to reuse objects based on bitmap contents have been tightened to avoid "
"race condition even when multiple packs are involved.  (merge 62b3ec8a3f tb/"
"bitmap-fix-pack-reuse later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:321
msgid ""
"An earlier \"csum-file checksum does not have to be computed with sha1dc\" "
"topic had a few code paths that had initialized an implementation of a hash "
"function to be used by an unmatching hash by mistake, which have been "
"corrected.  (merge 599a63409b ps/weak-sha1-for-tail-sum-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.48.0.adoc:330
msgid ""
"Other code cleanup, docfix, build fix, etc.  (merge 77af53f56f aa/t7300-"
"modernize later to maint).  (merge dcd590a39d bf/t-readme-mention-reftable "
"later to maint).  (merge 68e3c69efa kh/trailer-in-glossary later to maint).  "
"(merge 91f88f76e6 tb/boundary-traversal-fix later to maint).  (merge "
"168ebb7159 jc/doc-error-message-guidelines later to maint).  (merge "
"18693d7d65 kh/doc-bundle-typofix later to maint).  (merge e2f5d3b491 kh/doc-"
"update-ref-grammofix later to maint).  (merge 8525e92886 mh/doc-windows-home-"
"env later to maint)."
msgstr ""
